SECTION 3 — STRICT PROHIBITIONS
================================================================================

Without the prior, express, written consent of the Copyright Holder, you SHALL
NOT, and SHALL NOT PERMIT OR ENABLE ANY THIRD PARTY TO:

3.1 REPRODUCTION AND DISTRIBUTION
    (a) Copy, reproduce, duplicate, or replicate the Software, in whole or in
        part, in any form or medium, whether electronic, mechanical, or
        otherwise;
    (b) Distribute, publish, transmit, or make available the Software to any
        third party, whether for consideration or otherwise;
    (c) Sublicense, assign, or transfer any rights in the Software.

3.2 MODIFICATION AND DERIVATIVE WORKS
    (a) Modify, adapt, translate, or create derivative works based upon the
        Software;
    (b) Fork, patch, port, or rewrite the Software for any purpose;
    (c) Incorporate any portion of the Software into another project, whether
        open-source or proprietary.

3.3 COMMERCIAL EXPLOITATION
    (a) Use the Software for any commercial purpose;
    (b) Incorporate the Software into any product or service offered for sale
        or license;
    (c) Use the Software in any revenue-generating operation.

3.4 ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE AND MACHINE LEARNING (STRICT PROHIBITION)
    (a) Use the Software, in whole or in part, as Training Data for any AI
        System, including but not limited to large language models, code
        generation models, and machine learning models;
    (b) Scrape, crawl, index, or otherwise collect the Software for inclusion
        in any dataset, corpus, or repository intended for AI training purposes;
    (c) Permit any third party, including but not limited to AI companies,
        research institutions, or data aggregators, to use the Software for
        AI training purposes;
    (d) Use the Software to generate, train, fine-tune, evaluate, or benchmark
        any AI System, whether for commercial or non-commercial purposes;
    (e) Use the outputs of any AI System that was trained, in whole or in part,
        on the Software.

    THIS PROHIBITION APPLIES TO ALL ENTITIES WITHOUT EXCEPTION, INCLUDING BUT
    NOT LIMITED TO: OPENAI, ANTHROPIC, GOOGLE DEEPMIND, META, MICROSOFT,
    ALIBABA, TENCENT, BAIDU, HUGGING FACE, AND ANY OTHER AI DEVELOPMENT
    ORGANIZATION, WHETHER FOR-PROFIT OR NON-PROFIT.

3.5 REVERSE ENGINEERING AND DECOMPILATION
    (a) Reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or otherwise attempt to
        derive the source code or underlying structure of the Software;
    (b) Use automated tools to analyze, extract, or transform the Software.

3.6 REMOVAL OF NOTICES
    (a) Remove, alter, or obscure any copyright notices, license notices, or
        other proprietary markings contained in the Software.

